Z||000004||loafer87gt||02-11-2001||07:39 PM||||I change beer brands depending on the season. My winter beer is Molson Canadian, but in summer I'm partial to Miller Genuine Draft or Sol (better than Corono IMHO). Probably the tastiest beer I have ever had in my life was from a French brewing company called "Trois Pistols". It was a 9% beer and had a bunch of witchcraft stuff on the bottle. I would advise everyone to stay away from La Fin du Monde (End of the world). Thats how I felt in the morning after drinking one of their 1 litres bottles of the stuff. Heres the link to their brewery, they have a bunch of award winning brews:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.unibroue.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.unibroue.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||02-11-2001||07:47 PM||||Too many to remember.  And -- in a lifetime of research -- I haven't tried them all yet.<P><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI><B>Lager</B> - Sam Adams is hard to beat<BR>-<BR><LI><B>English ale</B> - Too many to list, but particularly Whitbread, Spitfire, Fuller's ESB, King & Barnes Challenger<BR>-<BR><LI><B>Scotch ale</B> - McEwans or Road Dog<BR>-<BR><LI><B>Stout</B> - Blind Man or Dogwood (both local)<BR>-<BR><LI><B>Porter</B> - Sweetwater (local) or Anchor<BR></UL><P>I could go on, but I'd rather have a beer.<BR>||||reg||1
