Z||000015||2birds||02-11-2001||11:16 PM||||I don't drink much, so I don't mind spending a bit more for something good. My favorite is Guinness, but only if I can get on tap.<P>Bottled, Michelob Dark if I can find it, or Michelob Amber Bock will substitute here in the South.<P>Sam Adams Cherry Wheat for a lighter brew.<P>I drank a lot of some local brew (Keith's, maybe?) when I made a port call in Halifax.  Pretty good stuff.  I found a lot of good brews in England (Tennent's, for one), and the Netherlands (Oranjeboom), too.  The Monks in Belgium and the Netherlands make some wicked brews, too.||||reg||1
