Z||000033||Fformula88||02-12-2001||07:09 PM||||Since many of our American forum members do not live close enough to experience Canadian Beer on both sides of the border, I feel its my duty to give a comparison.  Of course I am biased because my fav. beer is already Blue (Labatts Blue for those of you who don't know what I mean!).  Its good everywhere, but Canadian beer is much better across the border.  I don't know why... maybe its sits too long in customs, or maybe it just losses its taste outside of its country.  I try to stay away from the commonAmerican stuff... bud, coors etc.  Sam Adams would probably be my second choice.<P>BTW, do they air the Labatte Bear commercials in Canada?  One of the first ones, the Bear pointed out that Canada was a whole country north of Buffalo!  As if we have it so bad (Ok, 180 inches of snow per winter... we do!).  They are funny!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">      <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2m6<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000034||TheFiero64||02-13-2001||03:31 PM||||I love those commercials.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000035||kslish||02-14-2001||05:22 PM||||Being a Pittsburgher, my main beer staple is Iron City.  Followed closely by Yuengling for when I want a darker brew.  Rolling Rock is in third (made in good old Latrobe, PA).  Then maybe MGD and Killian's Red.<P>You couldn't pay me to drink Budwiser, it makes my stomach sick.<P>Haven't touched Beast since I was in college a few years back..... that and Old English 300 (the 40 ounce bottles of course).  Money was short back then.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>I used to like Corona but gave up drinking it after a friend of mine toured a brewery in Mexico and told me of what he saw there.  Not the best of conditions.<P>Ken S.<BR>||||reg||1
